From 0f2a9c6f0bf5fcaff92d1d012b97105308b7240b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:29:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: independent reference in the tests, shared
 build script

The reference library of the `generic` interface was built in the same
call of MFront as the tested library, with the tested compiler. The
compilers translating host and device code in a single pass (nvc++
-stdpar=gpu and -mp=gpu, AdaptiveCpp) define TFEL_DEVICE_CODE in host
code too: for those configurations, the tests compared the device code
paths to themselves.

The new build-libraries.sh script, shared by the tests of all the
configurations:
- builds the reference library with the `generic` interface and the
  default compiler of MFront, in the `reference` directory (the
  MFRONT_GPB_REFERENCE_CONFIGURATION_FILE environment variable may give
  another configuration file);
- builds the tested libraries with the `generic` and `generic-parallel`
  interfaces and the configuration file of the tested configuration,
  which checks that both interfaces can be used together.

The list of the test behaviours is now given once, in this script,
instead of being repeated in the fifteen test files.
